From 85dd8b59a363574e90022cd601ac5708e6f4e282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 15:24:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] board: freescale: gateway-dk: add per-component
 self-tests

Adds the ten per-chip self-test modules invoked from misc_init_r() via
the harness in the previous patch. Each one probes its target through
the I2C mux and reports PASS/FAIL with a small detail string:

  - clock_gen.c        - 6V49205B clock generator (Sys_CCB output)
  - ddr_sanity.c       - bit-pattern probe of DDR4 banks 0 and 1
  - fan_controller.c   - EMC2302 fan controller, tach + RPM
  - led_controller.c   - LP5810A status LED (also surfaces the
                         aggregate self-test verdict on the front
                         panel via lp5810a_set_status())
  - retimer.c          - DS100DF410 SerDes retimer device ID
  - rtc.c              - PCF2131 real-time clock
  - sfp_i2c_mux.c      - resets the SFP-side PCA9545 mux into a
                         known-good state
  - temp_sensors.c     - TMP431 CPU and board temperature
  - typec_controller.c - HD3SS3220/TUSB322 USB Type-C controller
  - voltage_sensors.c  - eight INA234 rails behind a PCA9545

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific]

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
